<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Divorce Petition — Advocates Hub Legal Draft</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: 'Calibri', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #1e293b; margin: 30px; }
  .header-box { border: 2px solid #1e3a8a; background: #eff6ff; padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px; text-align: center; }
  .header-box h1 { margin: 0 0 6px 0; color: #1e3a8a; font-size: 18pt; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .header-box p { margin: 0; color: #475569; font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold; }
  .checklist-box { border: 1px solid #d97706; background: #fffbeb; padding: 14px 18px; border-radius: 6px; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .checklist-box h3 { margin: 0 0 10px 0; color: #b45309; font-size: 12pt; }
  .chk-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 6px; }
  .chk-table th, .chk-table td { border: 1px solid #fde68a; padding: 7px 10px; font-size: 9.5pt; text-align: left; }
  .chk-table th { background: #fef3c7; color: #92400e; width: 26%; }
  .draft-title { text-align: center; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; margin: 24px 0 16px 0; color: #0f172a; text-decoration: underline; }
  .draft-body { white-space: pre-wrap; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.65; color: #0f172a; }
  .footer-note { margin-top: 36px; border-top: 1px solid #94a3b8; padding-top: 10px; font-size: 8.5pt; color: #64748b; text-align: center; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="header-box">
  <h1>ADVOCATES HUB — VERIFIED LEGAL DRAFT</h1>
  <p>Standard Indian Legal & Judicial Format • Verified by Legal Practitioners</p>
</div>

<div class="checklist-box">
  <h3>⚡ Statutory Execution Checklist & Mandatory Requirements</h3>
  <table class="chk-table">
    <tr><th>Applicable Statute</th><td>Section 13-B Hindu Marriage Act 1955 / Section 28 Special Marriage Act 1954</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Stamp Duty</th><td><strong>Court Fee Stamps as per Karnataka Court Fees and Suits Valuation Act (Nominal ₹20-₹100)</strong></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Registration</th><td>Filed before the Principal Family Court Judge in District of jurisdiction</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Notarization</th><td>Supporting Affidavits must be sworn before Oath Commissioner / Notary Public</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Jurisdiction</th><td>Family Court where marriage was solemnized, where parties last resided together, or where wife resides</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Limitation</th><td>Parties must have lived separately for a period of at least 1 (one) year before filing</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Required Enclosures</th><td>Original Marriage Certificate / Wedding Card / Photos; Aadhaar Cards and Passport Size Photographs of both Spouses; Proof of Separation (Addresses reflecting separate living for 1+ year); Settlement Agreement / Terms of Compromise (Alimony, Stridhan, Child Custody)</td></tr>
  </table>
</div>

<div class="draft-title">DIVORCE PETITION</div>
<div class="draft-body">IN THE PRINCIPAL FAMILY COURT AT ________________________, KARNATAKA
M.C. NO. ___________ OF 2026

IN THE MATTER OF:
PETITION UNDER SECTION 13-B OF THE HINDU MARRIAGE ACT, 1955 FOR DISSOLUTION OF MARRIAGE BY MUTUAL CONSENT

BETWEEN:
1. __________________________________________________ (Husband / First Petitioner)
   Age: _____ Years, S/o ________________________________
   Residing at: _________________________________________

                                    AND
2. __________________________________________________ (Wife / Second Petitioner)
   Age: _____ Years, D/o ________________________________
   Residing at: _________________________________________

MOST RESPECTFULLY SHOWETH:
1. That marriage between Petitioners was solemnized on ___/___/____ at ________________________ as per Hindu Vedic rites and customs.
2. That after marriage, Petitioners resided together as husband and wife. No children were born / children details: ________________________________.
3. That due to temperamental differences, Petitioners could not adjust and have been living separately since ___/___/____ (more than 1 year).
4. That all mediation efforts failed, and both parties have voluntarily decided to dissolve their marriage by mutual consent without any coercion or undue influence.
5. SETTLEMENT TERMS:
   (a) Permanent Alimony: First Petitioner has paid a sum of Rs. ____________/- in full and final settlement.
   (b) Stridhan & Articles: All gold jewellery and personal effects have been exchanged and returned.
   (c) Future Claims: Neither party shall make any future financial or property claims against the other.

PRAYER:
Wherefore, Petitioners pray that this Hon'ble Court may be pleased to pass a Decree of Dissolution of Marriage by mutual consent dissolving the marriage solemnized on ___/___/____.

FIRST PETITIONER: ____________________       SECOND PETITIONER: ____________________
VERIFICATION & SWORN AFFIDAVITS ATTACHED</div>

<div class="footer-note">
  Downloaded from Advocates Hub (https://advocateshub.in) • Valid across Karnataka & India
</div>
</body>
</html>